// Arithmetic and division - constant folding plus the magic-number paths.
//
// This used to be a list of constant expressions evaluated once, which made it
// not a benchmark at all: the whole program folded to a single `print` of a
// literal, so 0.01s of process startup was the entire measurement and every
// optimization level tied. A constant-folding test belongs in the golden suite,
// and folding is still what the head of this does.
//
// The loop is what makes it measurable. `k` comes from the clock, so nothing in
// the body can be folded away, and the divisors are loop-invariant so the
// magic-number divide is hoisted out (LICM, -O2) rather than recomputed 20M
// times -- which is the thing worth watching, since a hoisted expression that
// the loop varies was exactly the LICM bug `test-all` exists to catch.
int main() {
    var s = 0;
    s += 2 + 3 * 4 + (5 - 1) * 2;
    s += 100 / 5 + 100 % 7;
    s += 7 * 6 - 2;
    s += 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5;

    var k = 12345;
    var d = 1000000007;
    var i = 0;
    while (i < 20000000) {
        s = (s + k * 7 + i / 3) % d;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    print(s);
    return 0;
}
